 ## Overview
-Differential Ratio Tracing (DRT) is a sampling strategy for estimating gradients of the radiative transfer equation with respect to medium density in differentiable volume rendering [S1]. It solves the problem of biased and high-variance gradients produced by standard volumetric free-flight sampling (e.g., delta tracking) by sampling distances proportional to the unweighted transmittance rather than extinction-weighted transmittance [S1]. Unlike [Single-Scattering Differentiable Volume Rendering](4143-single-scattering-differentiable-volume-rendering.md), which relies on pre-computed view-independent terms, DRT is a Monte Carlo estimator that must recompute gradients for each view [S2]. It is designed for physically-based scattering and absorbing volumes, as opposed to NeRF-style emissive volumes [S1].
