 - **Strengths**: Unbiased, yields low-variance gradients, and handles empty/low-density regions better than standard free-flight sampling [S1].
 - **Limitations**: Must recompute gradients for each view, unlike pre-computed methods [S2]. More expensive than single-scattering methods at high sample counts [S2].
-- **When to Use**: When using physically-based scattering and absorbing volumes and when gradient variance in low-density regions is a concern [S1]. When using [Single-Scattering Differentiable Volume Rendering](4143-single-scattering-differentiable-volume-rendering.md) is not feasible due to multiple scattering or complex geometry.
